ark can be answered."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Epilogue: The Light Kept', 'text': "Years later, Sarah Okafor still walks the town of Gray's End at night, checking the rooms the way you check on sleeping children. The nursery is a study now. The cold spot is just a draft. Mostly.\n\nSometimes a child's drawing dated tomorrow catches the light oddly, and Sarah Okafor feels the old chill. Then Sarah Okafor touches it, whole and quiet, and remembers the choice: to face it, to mend it, to stay.\n\nAnd the town of Gray's End stands in its fog, ordinary and beloved, a house like any other — except that once, it was haunted, and once, someone stayed. That makes all the difference."}]}

